&ldquo;I swan, you&rsquo;ve took me mighty unexpected, William! It sort of started the
      shivers. Fact is, I was thinkin&rsquo; so busy about makin&rsquo; things comfortable for the others, I
      hadn&rsquo;t thought about being buried myself.&rdquo;

&ldquo;Life&rsquo;s on&rsquo;y a fleetin&rsquo; show, John, as the sayin&rsquo; is.
      We&rsquo;ve all got to go, sooner or later. To go with a clean record&rsquo;s the main thing. Fact is, it&rsquo;s
      the on&rsquo;y thing worth strivin&rsquo; for, John.&rdquo;

&ldquo;All right, set your name down here, John,under E. Now, if you don&rsquo;t
      mind payin&rsquo; me your share of the fourteen dollars, John, while we&rsquo;re
      on the business, everything&rsquo;s fixed.&rdquo;

Twice since we left port our engines have stopped for a couple of minutes
      at a time. Now they stop again. Says the pale young man, meditatively,
      &ldquo;There!&mdash;that engineer is sitting down to rest again.&rdquo;

The next morning, at what seemed a very early hour, the little white
      table-waiter appeared suddenly in my room and shot a single word out of
      himself &ldquo;Breakfast!&rdquo;

We passed a roadside grocery with a sign up, &ldquo;Potatoes Wanted.&rdquo;
      An ignorant stranger, doubtless. He could not have gone thirty steps from
      his place without finding plenty of them.
